* PIC18F4x5x Pin Definitions file
* Generated from Microchip DS39632E (PIC18F2455/2550/4455/4550 Data Sheet)
* Package: 40-Pin PDIP
*
* Layout convention: VDD is the first record (top-left of symbol),
* SIMCLK is the last record of the left column (bottom-left),
* VSS is the last record overall (bottom-right).
* Middle pins (everything except VDD/SIMCLK/VSS) are sorted in ascending
* alphabetical/register order, so pins sharing a port prefix (RA, RB,
* RC, RD, RE) group together and sort ascending by pin number within
* the group. Non-port utility pins (OSC1, VUSB) fall into their natural
* alphabetical position in that same sort.
* Total records = 39 (odd), so one X spacer is inserted before SIMCLK
* to bring the total to 40 -- an exact 20/20 left/right split, with no
* dependence on how QSymGen3 rounds size/2.
D Microchip PIC18F4455/4550 40-pin, USB, Enhanced Flash microcontroller
P PIC18F4455 PIC18F4550

* --- Left column (20 records): VDD ... SIMCLK ---
V VDD
* NOTE: pin 32 is a second physical VDD pin (same net as pin 11's VDD).
* No separate record is created for it -- see the pitfall on duplicate
* pin names.

I OSC1 CLKI                     * pin 13, input-only, no GPIO alt function

* PORTA is a bidirectional I/O port -- RA0-RA5 all classified B.
B RA0 AN0                       * pin 2
B RA1 AN1                       * pin 3
B RA2 AN2/VREF-/CVREF           * pin 4
B RA3 AN3/VREF+                 * pin 5
B RA4 T0CKI/C1OUT/RCV           * pin 6
B RA5 AN4/SS/HLVDIN/C2OUT       * pin 7

* Pin 14 - OSC2/CLKO/RA6 -- FLAGGED: oscillator-mode dependent. RA6 is
* only available as GPIO when the device is configured for an internal
* oscillator; otherwise this pin is OSC2/CLKO (both outputs). Classified
* B for simulation flexibility, but this needs a human decision based on
* the target oscillator configuration.
B RA6 OSC2/CLKO

* PORTB is a bidirectional I/O port -- RB0-RB7 all classified B.
B RB0 AN12/INT0/FLT0/SDI/SDA    * pin 33
B RB1 AN10/INT1/SCK/SCL         * pin 34
B RB2 AN8/INT2/VMO              * pin 35
B RB3 AN9/CCP2/VPO              * pin 36
B RB4 AN11/KBI0/CSSPP           * pin 37
B RB5 KBI1/PGM                  * pin 38
B RB6 KBI2/PGC                  * pin 39
B RB7 KBI3/PGD                  * pin 40

* PORTC is a bidirectional I/O port (see RC4/RC5 exceptions below).
B RC0 T1OSO/T13CKI              * pin 15

* Spacer added to make the total record count even (40), so the
* left/right column split is exactly 20/20 -- no dependence on how
* QSymGen3 rounds size/2. This guarantees SIMCLK is the last (bottom)
* entry of the left column.
X

K SIMCLK

* --- Right column (20 records): RC1 ... VSS ---
B RC1 T1OSI/CCP2/UOE            * pin 16
B RC2 CCP1/P1A                  * pin 17

* Pins 23-24 - RC4/D-/VM, RC5/D+/VP -- FLAGGED: pin-level exceptions to
* "PORTC is a bidirectional I/O port". Both are documented as
* input-only digital pins (dedicated USB D-/D+ lines). Classified I,
* not B.
I RC4 D-/VM                     * pin 23
I RC5 D+/VP                     * pin 24

B RC6 TX/CK                     * pin 25
B RC7 RX/DT/SDO                 * pin 26

* PORTD is a bidirectional I/O port or Streaming Parallel Port.
B RD0 SPP0                      * pin 19
B RD1 SPP1                      * pin 20
B RD2 SPP2                      * pin 21
B RD3 SPP3                      * pin 22
B RD4 SPP4                      * pin 27
B RD5 SPP5/P1B                  * pin 28
B RD6 SPP6/P1C                  * pin 29
B RD7 SPP7/P1D                  * pin 30

* PORTE is a bidirectional I/O port (see RE3 exception below).
B RE0 AN5/CK1SPP                * pin 8
B RE1 AN6/CK2SPP                * pin 9
B RE2 AN7/OESPP                 * pin 10

* Pin 1 - MCLR/VPP/RE3 -- FLAGGED: pin-level exception to "PORTE is
* bidirectional"; RE3 is documented as input-only on this shared pin
* (unlike RE0-RE2), and MCLR/VPP are both inputs. Classified I, not B.
I RE3 MCLR/VPP

* Pin 18 - VUSB -- FLAGGED: internal 3.3V USB regulator output, not a
* standard VDD supply pin. Classified O (regulator output), not V.
O VUSB

G VSS
* NOTE: pin 31 is a second physical VSS pin (same net as pin 12's VSS).
* No separate record is created for it -- see the pitfall on duplicate
* pin names.
